{"id": "EUVD-2026-101570", "enisaUuid": "2e4dfd45-9ce3-3e53-91f8-e8693d4a01f1", "description": "Databasus 3.7.0 through 3.61.0 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to brute-force password reset codes via POST /api/v1/users/reset-password. Attackers can request a six-digit code for a known email, then guess it without rate limiting, lockout, or invalidation to take over accounts, including administrators.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T18:47:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:47:54", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/databasus-password-reset-code-brute-force", "https://github.com/databasus/databasus/blob/9ee25ed8f47b1b537468417e1bb52ed2d76218a0/backend/internal/features/users/services/user_services.go#L637", "https://github.com/databasus/databasus", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/databasus-3.7.0-through-3.61.0-account-takeover-via-password-reset-brute-force"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110770", "GHSA-jj5w-98p7-g6gj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8ca691f0-706b-3922-9ff9-fbf0d93a574f", "product": {"name": "databasus", "vendor": {"name": "databasus"}}, "product_version": "3.7.0 \u22643.61.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fa67b77f-6366-3a22-8610-137a341e82d2", "vendor": {"name": "databasus"}}], "isExploited": false}